  "interpretation": [
    "The current MeshTransformer is materially better than a non-spatial boundary mean and transfers from the training geometry family to unseen geometry modes without a large additional penalty.",
    "This trained MeshTransformer configuration learns harmonic modes one and two but fails on trained modes three and four under the mixed physical-area objective; equal boundary variance does not equalize interior solution energy.",
    "The dense invariant pair kernel is much more accurate but has quadratic source-query cost and still extrapolates poorly to unseen high boundary frequencies.",
    "Low supervised value error does not imply PDE fidelity: the pair kernel has the best value error and the worst autograd Laplacian residual.",
    "The learned core satisfies similarity covariance to ordinary fp32 roundoff and remains stable under boundary quadrature refinement.",
    "The next controlled experiment should equalize solution-space energy or train pure modes before attributing the remaining gap to representation; higher-order equivariant representations and controlled nonseparable kernels are principled follow-ups."
  ]
